<span style="font-size:110%">'''Dispute overview'''</span>
* ''Can you give us a quick explanation of what is going on? What is the issue you are bringing here?''

A large, ongoing debate on <strike>copyright ownership</strike> issues regarding the usage of the terms "reprint," "first serial rights," and "originally published in" to describe a few stories (specifically [[Gilgamesh in the Outback]] and Newton Sleep) in a larger series called [[Heroes in Hell]] is occurring at [[Talk:Heroes in Hell|its talk page]].  [[User:Hullaballoo Wolfowitz|Hullaballoo Wolfowitz]] argues that these stories were reprints from a prior magazine publication based on the sources he has found (some unreliable like this: [http://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?41374], but others reliable like this: [http://books.google.com/books?id=QznkqRQCuuMC&q=%22gilgamesh+in+the+outback%22&dq=%22gilgamesh+in+the+outback%22&hl=en&ei=zvRDTp7lH8bo0QHp_IT1CQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CEgQ6AEwBg] and [http://www.majipoor.com/work.php?id=377 the author of ''Gilgamesh''<nowiki>'s</nowiki> own website]).  On the other hand, several other editors have argued that the use of the term "reprint" or saying that it is "originally published" in the magazine is misleading and wrongly suggests the original copyright is not owned by the series author, Janet Morris.  Editors argue more accurately would be to say that the magazine had "first serial" rights.  However, as of yet, no source points to the magazine having any such rights.  They also argue that the story was intended to be written for the series, and as such, the magazine article is merely promotional, but not copyrighted.  All of these arguments, however, lack sources.  It is unclear whether it is standard for primary sources to provide this kind of "first serial" copyright information.  Edit warring related to the above issues have occurred in the past week on both pages: [http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Heroes_in_Hell&diff=444143000&oldid=444142667], [http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Heroes_in_Hell&diff=444156830&oldid=444156355], [http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Gilgamesh_in_the_Outback&action=historysubmit&diff=444134483&oldid=436474478], [http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Gilgamesh_in_the_Outback&diff=444365229&oldid=444331696], [http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Gilgamesh_in_the_Outback&diff=444370337&oldid=444365637]

